{title: 089 - Let All on Earth Their Voices Raise}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #089 • OLD 113TH • 8.8.6.8.8.6}
{lyricist: Isaac Watts on}
{composer: Matthaus Greiter}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 89}
{meta: tune OLD 113TH}
{meta: meter 8.8.6.8.8.6}
{meta: category God the Father - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D/F#]Let all [A]the [D/A]earth their voices [F#m/C#]raise,
[Em/B]To [D/A]sing [A]the [D/A]great [E]Jehovah's [A]praise,
[D/A]And bless His [Em/B]holy [D/F#]name:
[D/A]His glory [A]let the people know,
[D/A]His [Bm]wonders [A]to [G#m]the [A]nations [Em/G]show,
[G]His saving [Em/B]grace [A]proclaim.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D/F#]He framed [A]the [D/A]globe; He built [Em/B]the [F#m/C#]sky;
[Em/B]He [D/A]made [A]the [D/A]shining [A/E]worlds [G]on [A]high,
[D/A]And reigns in [Em/B]glory [D/F#]there:
[D/A]His beams are [A]majesty [G#m]and [A]light;
[D/A]His [Bm]beauties, [A]how divinely [Em/G]bright!
[G]His dwelling [Em/B]place, [A]how [D/F#]fair!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D/F#]Come, the [A]great [D/A]day, the glorious [F#m/C#]hour,
[Em/B]When [D/A]earth [A]shall [D/A]feel His [A/E]saving [G]power,
[D/A]All nations [Em/B]fear [A]His [D/F#]name;
[D/A]Then shall the [A]race of men [G#m]confess
[D/A]The [Bm]beauty [A]of [G#m]His [A]holiness,
[G]His saving [Em/B]grace [A]proclaim.
{end_of_verse}
